id: pm-jqgkis
title: Preserve budget omission types across union SDK option shapes
description: "PmReadOutputResultFor checks outputBudget, outputSession and outputCursor against keyof Options. For a union such as {limit:string}|{outputBudget:number}, keyof retains only shared keys, so a valid budgeted runtime branch is typed as an ordinary result. Distribute the return-type calculation across option variants and retain correct first-page, producer-continuation and omission narrowing."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: output-contracts,sdk,types
created_at: "2026-10-21T04:23:02.916Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:31.744Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:29.913Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T05:41:29.913Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A union containing any budget-capable variant retains PmReadOutputBudgetExceeded; no-control variants preserve ordinary results; union producer and budget variants compose safely; source and packed public declaration fixtures fail before and pass after the correction
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Distribute option-sensitive read results across union variants before key inspection, retaining every possible budget, session, output-cursor omission and producer continuation shape without changing serialized payloads."
expected_result: "Every possible omission stays visible to a typed caller using union-shaped options, and useful rows remain accessible after narrowing."
actual_result: "All final PM-linked compiler checks and the shared source and actual-tarball public declaration fixture pass, including forbidden unsafe access for budget/session/output-cursor unions and composed producer-budget variants. Complete accepted source coverage is exact 100/100/100/100. The isolated pre-fix compiler fails the independent expectations."
